// L'Asie (the update « pays-asie »; the Middle East and Oceania are their own): the capitals and the great cities
// of East, South, Southeast and Central Asia. In depth (several communes): Pékin (and the Great Wall at Badaling),
// Shanghai, Canton and Xiaobei, its quarter of West African traders; Tokyo, Osaka, Kyoto; New Delhi, Mumbai,
// Bangalore; Séoul; Bangkok; Hanoï, Hô Chi Minh-Ville; Jakarta, Bali; Singapour; Kuala Lumpur; Manille. Then Hong
// Kong, Taipei, Islamabad, Karachi, Dacca, Colombo, Katmandou, Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Vientiane, Rangoun,
// Naypyidaw, Oulan-Bator, Astana, Almaty, Tachkent, Samarcande, Malé, Bandar Seri Begawan and Thimphou. Each with
// its city hall, its airport (Air Lagune flies there, game/asie.go) and its famous places, positioned from
// OpenStreetMap (Nominatim, 26 November 2026) where it found them, else where they are known to be (Approx); the
// restaurants, clubs, barbers and hotels are the game's. Generated (scratch spec) like world/europe.go.
//
// Roads: through land borders only (Borders, europe.go's chain: Asia joins Europe's Russia and, through the
// Middle East, Turkey). No road to the islands (Japan's cities join each other only; the Philippines, Taiwan,
// Sri Lanka, the Maldives, Bali, Brunei on Borneo, Java's Jakarta alone), nor across the Korean border; Singapore
// joins Malaysia by the causeway.

